-- #1557 A-3.5c -- THE BYSTANDER, the half no drain fixture can cover.
--
-- AGENTS.md's rule for any change that re-keys a program-global table: the required
-- fixture is *"feature + UNRELATED code still behaves"*, not *"feature works"*. This
-- graph contains exactly the collision A-3.5c's cycle walk was re-keyed for -- two
-- unrelated modules, each declaring an interface `Same` AND an interface `Base` --
-- and it is entirely well-formed. Every file's bucket must be `[]`.
--
-- HOW EACH ARM CAN FAIL, which is what makes this an assertion rather than a
-- decoration:
--   * Collapse the four interfaces onto their two bare names and the super edges
--     read `Same -> Base` (from `pmod`) and `Base -> Same` (from `qmod`): a cycle
--     that does not exist. A re-key that keyed on the SPELLING, or a `done`/`path`
--     set still keyed on a bare name, gains a spurious T-CYCLIC-SUPERINTERFACE here.
--   * Nothing below mentions `Same`, `Base`, `psf`, `pbf`, `qsf` or `qbf`. Only the
--     two functions are imported, so this file answers AGENTS.md's *"what happens to
--     a program that never touches the table"* directly.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT IT CANNOT CATCH, stated so it is not read as covering more than it does:
-- it detects an edge that WRONGLY MEETS another module's row. It cannot detect an
-- edge that NEVER MEETS its own row -- a write-side/read-side identity disagreement
-- would leave the walk finding nothing and every bucket here `[]`. That direction is
-- `1557_a35c_cycle_masked_by_samespelled/`, which goes silent exactly when this one
-- cannot. The set is the assertion; no single member is.
import pmod.{pfn}
import qmod.{qfn}

main = println (qfn (pfn 1))
